        "pl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "bf578359-9c0f-3582-b609-ccda7b103739",
                "word": "widzimisię",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "pl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "28835696-2da1-35f3-951e-122b0042355c",
                        "entry_id": "bf578359-9c0f-3582-b609-ccda7b103739",
                        "glosses": [
                            "czyjś pogląd nieliczący się z niczym"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2855f5a9-b53e-45c3-bd33-4b2e779b7079",
                                "sense_id": "28835696-2da1-35f3-951e-122b0042355c",
                                "text": "Bonhart to nieobliczalny sadysta. (…) W zależności od widzimisię pojmaną dziewczynę gotów zakatować albo porwać, by kazać jej walczyć na arenach"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "35072263-6eb0-42a5-96a0-6e48e2b7a030",
                                "sense_id": "28835696-2da1-35f3-951e-122b0042355c",
                                "text": "Przeorganizowała kuchnię podług własnego widzimisię: poprzekładała rzeczy w szufladach, zgarnęła porcelanowe skorupy, ofiary furii Maurycego, znalazła i schowała na lepszą godzinę jego podarte memuary, kazała wywietrzyć pościel i osiarkowała piwnicę"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "69555317-bfab-4f60-a05f-c3efe4a1670c",
                        "source_entry_id": "bf578359-9c0f-3582-b609-ccda7b103739",
                        "source_sense_id": "28835696-2da1-35f3-951e-122b0042355c",
                        "target_lang_word": "whim",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "whim",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "278fa71e-d392-3bb6-b0ed-1b262626f305",
                                        "entry_id": "ff1fd901-60b4-32d7-95e0-a7807734cfd3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fanciful impulse, or sudden change of idea."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e896ede-beb5-441f-9a84-fe9f250d66ac",
                                                "sense_id": "278fa71e-d392-3bb6-b0ed-1b262626f305",
                                                "text": "Let ev’ry Man enjoy his whim; / What’s He to Me, or I to him?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b51de581-69ed-47ee-890d-e8d3a3283099",
                                                "sense_id": "278fa71e-d392-3bb6-b0ed-1b262626f305",
                                                "text": "The king was tired of this whim of hers long ago, and thought she ought to get married like other people; there was nothing she need wait for, she was old enough and she would not be any richer either, for she was to have half the kingdom, which she inherited after her mother."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f38383f-7e86-48d8-ab88-bf281d714d64",
                                                "sense_id": "278fa71e-d392-3bb6-b0ed-1b262626f305",
                                                "text": "“You’re either with me or you’re against me” became Dany’s credo, and those against her were an ever-changing multitude to be determined solely by her whims."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d78c190-eaea-4acf-ac9b-d6b4661d2691",
                                                "sense_id": "278fa71e-d392-3bb6-b0ed-1b262626f305",
                                                "text": "He also disagreed with the idea of cancelling projects \"completely at the whim of an individual Prime Minister,\" citing Rishi Sunak's decision to cancel HS2 north of Handsacre Junction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c84913e7-275a-399d-826b-59c394c8ead4",
                                        "entry_id": "ff1fd901-60b4-32d7-95e0-a7807734cfd3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large capstan or vertical drum turned by horse power or steam power, for raising ore or water, etc., from mines, or for other purposes"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "whim",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb0330d1-8ee0-3a63-b70b-a4e64b1dc4e7",
                                        "entry_id": "6c80e1ef-c372-375b-8217-171a17ce2b30",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be seized with a whim; to be capricious."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "whim",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e11dc728-b000-32a2-84a4-7f25824df9db",
                                        "entry_id": "db4f4598-d06d-3f3d-a33d-48ab561b2dae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bird, the Eurasian wigeon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "68570a83-6433-430d-b8a9-8382204e6aac",
                        "source_entry_id": "bf578359-9c0f-3582-b609-ccda7b103739",
                        "source_sense_id": "28835696-2da1-35f3-951e-122b0042355c",
                        "target_lang_word": "caprice",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "caprice",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5506cde1-dbfe-36ee-a70b-df2ff68555ab",
                                        "entry_id": "3e63df55-a6db-30a8-9965-4a753eeb1e85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An impulsive, seemingly unmotivated action, change of mind, or notion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f0602b6-0c23-4512-99f1-6c7e607805ee",
                                                "sense_id": "5506cde1-dbfe-36ee-a70b-df2ff68555ab",
                                                "text": "Though more thoughtful than Madame de Mercœur, yet it asked far more knowledge of society—that wilderness of small intricacies—for her to penetrate into the motives of those who seemed so suddenly struck with her fascination; but she was too clear-headed to be deceived, and set it all down under one general belief in caprice."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38896eba-f60e-469e-a270-a76b7266c62a",
                                                "sense_id": "5506cde1-dbfe-36ee-a70b-df2ff68555ab",
                                                "text": "It would have been a great privilege to be the mistress of an old time-honoured mansion, to call oaks and elms her own, to know that acres of gardens were submitted to her caprices, to look at herds of cows and oxen, and be aware that they lowed on her own pastures."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89e1d7e9-e983-49ff-a657-b0b65c5eb281",
                                                "sense_id": "5506cde1-dbfe-36ee-a70b-df2ff68555ab",
                                                "text": "She is said to be the finest swordswoman on the Continent. Yet, notwithstanding her caprices, she is a noble-minded woman."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "99e4c668-87d3-3fd8-86e0-d80fb0d1316f",
                                        "entry_id": "3e63df55-a6db-30a8-9965-4a753eeb1e85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A brief romance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "449c7576-922b-4a04-9460-99303efed123",
                                                "sense_id": "99e4c668-87d3-3fd8-86e0-d80fb0d1316f",
                                                "text": "The only difference between a caprice and a life-long passion is that a caprice lasts a little longer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc0ba891-f978-3ea4-b2a1-29b8a439c830",
                                        "entry_id": "3e63df55-a6db-30a8-9965-4a753eeb1e85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An unpredictable or sudden condition, change, or series of changes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3362f724-5d05-4153-8215-eb8235c44cc7",
                                                "sense_id": "dc0ba891-f978-3ea4-b2a1-29b8a439c830",
                                                "text": "After that we cast off all allegiance to immediate, tangible, and time-touched things, and entered a fantastic world of hushed unreality in which the narrow, ribbon-like road rose and fell and curved with an almost sentient and purposeful caprice amidst the tenantless green peaks and half-deserted valleys"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "359bfaa9-a354-3e65-b3a2-de8a76589901",
                                        "entry_id": "3e63df55-a6db-30a8-9965-4a753eeb1e85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A disposition to be impulsive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f55d58dd-6dfe-4278-b38e-2e52d79c7558",
                                                "sense_id": "359bfaa9-a354-3e65-b3a2-de8a76589901",
                                                "text": "Yet, Britain, vvhence this Caprice of thy Sons, / VVhich thro' their various ranks vvith fury runs? / The cauſe is plain, a cauſe vvhich vve muſt bleſs; / For Caprice is the Daughter of Succeſs, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "717b3646-76f1-45a5-9085-be689c8cb8cc",
                                                "sense_id": "359bfaa9-a354-3e65-b3a2-de8a76589901",
                                                "text": "This last act of our lives seldom belies the former tenor of them, for stupidity, caprice, and unmeaning spite. All that we seem to think of is to manage matters so […] as to do as little good, and to plague and disappoint as many people as possible."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "453cb4d5-3bee-45bb-9381-c3ca3f549662",
                                                "sense_id": "359bfaa9-a354-3e65-b3a2-de8a76589901",
                                                "text": "Skill, endurance, and perseverance may almost be called muscular virtues; and fatigue, velleity, caprice, ennui, restlessness, lack of control and poise, muscular faults."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9bd5bf9e-19ab-4c12-8cc2-6b8d07b3c815",
                                                "sense_id": "359bfaa9-a354-3e65-b3a2-de8a76589901",
                                                "text": "In selecting Bran Stark, the lords of Westeros are choosing to value these stories and memories above whatever other qualities might make a good ruler, and more specifically, put an end to the caprices of heritage that have allowed bloodlines to wreak havoc on good stewardship of these kingdoms."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4302c5af-6578-315f-95ec-a82d13a9d00e",
                                        "entry_id": "3e63df55-a6db-30a8-9965-4a753eeb1e85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A capriccio."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
